  "id": "dcf66469-be75-48b7-80ca-811a7cc5b066",
  "title": "Jharkhand Exam Protests Accuse Government of Betrayal Amid High Court Stays",
  "summary": "Protesters in Jharkhand accused the government of 'betrayal' after the High Court stayed several job exam cancellations, citing past issues with the government's handling of recruitment exams. The JMM-led government claims the decision is a response to systemic problems in the exam process, while protesters argue the government failed to properly defend their demands.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "The Jharkhand government canceled 22 recruitment exams, including those by the Jharkhand Public Service Commission and an outsourced agency, after protests and a 2-month ultimatum.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "The JMM-led government announced an inquiry into errors, citing past issues with the examination process, and claims the cancellation is a response to systemic problems.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "The Jharkhand High Court stayed several government notifications cancelling recruitment exams, which led to protests among successful candidates.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    }
  ],
